Why this is a feature on 8.2 rather than a bugfix on 8.1, and why `off()` comes with it.

`on()` documented that listeners are *"automatically cleared on detach"*. Removing that line changes a
stated contract, so it is a behavior change and belongs on the development branch. The docblock is
corrected in the second commit; it was still promising the old behavior.

The public API challenge for `off()`, run against the first commit alone:

```
after registering: fired=1
attempt 1, remove+add:      fired=2 (still firing)
attempt 2, candidate public methods: removeStyleClass, detach, clearRenderCache
attempt 3, $listeners visibility: private
```

Remove-and-add no longer releases a listener, which is the point of the first commit. No other public
method releases one either: `detach()` is `@internal`, and `removeStyleClass()` and `clearRenderCache()`
are unrelated. `$listeners` is private, so the only way left is reflection into internals the component
does not promise to keep. The attempt fails, which is what justifies adding the method.

One note for anyone weighing the old clearing behavior on leak grounds: it was not buying deterministic
teardown. Over 200 add/remove rounds with a self-capturing listener, the object graph leaves 6794
objects to the cycle collector with the clear and 7553 without. The widget and context graph is already
cyclic either way, so the collector has to run regardless.

