Comments addressed while rebasing on top of #65424: `off()` now uses the same comparison as `EventDispatcher::removeListener()`, so a first-class callable of the same method can be released; the docblock now states that `off()` removes every registration of the listener; and a new test pins that a widget out of the tree still fires its own listeners. A test also shows that an inline closure with a different binding is not matched, so the looser comparison cannot over-remove.
